<div style="background-color: #1a5276; color: white; padding: 20px; text-align: center; border-radius: 8px;">
    <h1 style="margin: 0;">Lesson Planner – Theme # ___ – Lesson # 5</h1>
    <p style="margin: 5px 0 0 0; font-size: 1.1em;">Complete this planner five times per theme, once per lesson (Lesson 1 through Lesson 5).</p>
</div>

<table style="border: 1px dashed #333; border-collapse: collapse; width: 100%; margin: 10px 0;">
    <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
        <td style="padding: 8px; border: 1px dashed #333; width: 50%;"><b>Lesson #:</b> 5</td>
        <td style="padding: 8px; border: 1px dashed #333; width: 50%;"><b>Skills Focus:</b> Mediation</td>
    </tr>
    <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
        <td style="padding: 8px; border: 1px dashed #333;"><b>Grade:</b> 6th Grade (CEFR: A2.1)</td>
        <td style="padding: 8px; border: 1px dashed #333;"><b>Scenario:</b> The Talents Around Us</td>
        <td style="padding: 8px; border: 1px dashed #333;"><b>Theme:</b> I Will Play the Drums in the Parade.</td>
    </tr>
    <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
        <td style="padding: 8px; border: 1px dashed #333;"><b>Date(s):</b> From ___ to ___</td>
        <td style="padding: 8px; border: 1px dashed #333;" colspan="2"><b>Learning Sequence Time:</b> 45–50 min</td>
    </tr>
    <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
        <td style="padding: 8px; border: 1px dashed #333;" colspan="3">
            <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Specific Objective:</b> Mediation: communication: Relay complex information from teachers to students. concept: Explain basic concepts using real-life examples.</p>
            <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Learning Outcome:</b> Mediation: Can explain basic concepts about Fiestas Patrias, using real-life examples and visuals (e.g., show a picture of students rehearsing a folkloric dance and write, 'Practice the dance steps.'). Can relay teacher instructions for Fiestas Patrias events by writing simple steps and using visuals (e.g., point to a clock drawing or a picture of the school gate and write, 'Meet at the school gate at 8 a.m.'). Can simplify parade preparation tasks using written steps and pictures (e.g., show an image of a student carrying the Panamanian flag in the parade and write, 'Hold the flag with both hands.').</p>
        </td>
    </tr>
</table>

<h2 style="color: #1a5276; text-align: center;">The Six Action-Oriented Approach (AOA) Lesson Stages</h2>
<table style="border: 1px dashed #333; border-collapse: collapse; width: 100%; margin: 10px 0;">
    <thead>
        <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333; background-color: #f2f2f2;">
            <th style="padding: 8px; border: 1px dashed #333; width: 33%; color: #1a5276;">Stage & Description</th>
            <th style="padding: 8px; border: 1px dashed #333; width: 34%; color: #1a5276;">Activities & Teacher Actions</th>
            <th style="padding: 8px; border: 1px dashed #333; width: 33%; color: #1a5276;">Estimated Date and Time</th>
        </tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
        <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
            <td style="padding: 8px; border: 1px dashed #333;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>STAGE 1 — Warm-up / Pre-task</b></p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Engagement, Modeling and Clarification</p>
            </td>
            <td style="padding: 8px; border: 1px dashed #333;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Warm-up:</b> The teacher displays various pictures of Fiestas Patrias events and preparations (e.g., students practicing a dance, a band marching, someone holding a flag, a child in a traditional costume). Students identify the pictures and say one word or a short sentence about what they see. Example: "Parade!", "They are dancing.", "Flag." This activates prior knowledge about the theme and scenario.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Modeling:</b> The teacher models relaying simple information using visuals. The teacher shows a complex instruction like "Students will collectively organize the artistic components of the Fiestas Patrias event." and then simplifies it by writing next to a picture of students collaborating: "We will prepare the art together." The teacher demonstrates using future simple: "I will play the drums." and 'can': "I can sing a patriotic song."</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Clarification (CCQs):</b></p>
                <ul>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"If I say 'Rehearse your dance steps carefully,' what will you do?" (Expected answer: "I will practice my dance steps.")</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"When we simplify, do we use long sentences or short, clear ones?" (Expected answer: "Short, clear ones.")</li>
                </ul>
            </td>
            <td style="padding: 8px; border: 1px dashed #333;">10 min</td>
        </tr>
        <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
            <td style="padding: 8px; border: 1px dashed #333;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>STAGE 2 — Presentation</b></p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Input of new language/content connected to Scenario: "The Talents Around Us"</p>
            </td>
            <td style="padding: 8px; border: 1px dashed #333;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Material:</b> The teacher presents a short "Documentary Guide" (a handout or projected text) for the Fiestas Patrias Celebration Documentary project. This guide contains slightly complex instructions and concepts related to filming and explaining traditions (e.g., "Interview the baton twirler about her skill and practice routine for the parade," "Explain the historical significance of the Panamanian flag in the celebration"). It also includes some example dialogue using the first conditional (e.g., "If you interview the performer, you will capture great moments."). The text incorporates vocabulary like 'documentary', 'celebration', 'traditions', 'event', 'practice', 'skill', 'costume', 'honor', 'parade', 'flag'.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Communicative Competence:</b> Mediation: communication: Relay complex information from teachers to students. concept: Explain basic concepts using real-life examples.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Comprehension tasks:</b> Students read the "Documentary Guide."</p>
                <ul>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Gist questions:</b> "What is the main goal of this guide?" (Expected answer: "To help us make a documentary.") "What is the documentary about?" (Expected answer: "Fiestas Patrias.")</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Information matching:</b> Match complex instructions from the guide to simple pictures the teacher draws on the board (e.g., match "Interview the baton twirler" to a drawing of a microphone and a twirler).</li>
                </ul>
            </td>
            <td style="padding: 8px; border: 1px dashed #333;">10 min</td>
        </tr>
        <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
            <td style="padding: 8px; border: 1px dashed #333;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>STAGE 3 — Preparation / Practice</b></p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Accuracy focus on Mediation</p>
            </td>
            <td style="padding: 8px; border: 1px dashed #333;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Communicative Skill & Content:</b> Students practice simplifying instructions and concepts related to the Fiestas Patrias Celebration Documentary, using future simple, first conditional, and 'can'. They will use vocabulary such as 'parade', 'flag', 'band', 'costume', 'practice', 'perform', 'talent', 'celebrate', 'honor', 'event', 'skill'. Pronunciation focus: minimal pairs /ʌ/ in 'fun' and /æ/ in 'band'.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Detailed Procedure:</b></p>
                <ul>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>1. Controlled practice: Simplify the Guide:</b> The teacher provides sentences from the "Documentary Guide." Students rewrite them using simpler language and add a small drawing or icon.
                        <ul>
                            <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Teacher: "The students must gather the traditional costumes for the dance performance."</li>
                            <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Student writes/says: "Get the costumes for the dance." (Draws a pollera.)</li>
                            <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Teacher: "If the band rehearses diligently, they will execute a superb performance."</li>
                            <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Student writes/says: "If the band practices, they will play well." (Draws a drum and a flute.)</li>
                        </ul>
                    </li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>2. Semi-controlled: Match and Explain:</b> The teacher projects a list of complex Fiestas Patrias concepts (e.g., "Abanderado," "Pollera," "Tamborito"). Students work individually to write a one-sentence simple explanation for each and draw a quick sketch. Then, they use the modal 'can' to express what they can do with this information.
                        <ul>
                            <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Teacher: "What is an Abanderado?"</li>
                            <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Student: "An Abanderado is an honor roll student who carries the flag. I can explain the Abanderado's role."</li>
                        </ul>
                    </li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>3. Pair interaction: Relay Instructions:</b> Students work in pairs. Student A receives a complex instruction for the documentary (e.g., "Record the preparation of the parade route, emphasizing safety protocols."). Student B must listen, then simplify the instruction, and write it down with visuals for their "documentary crew." Student A checks if the simplified instruction is clear and accurate. They switch roles. Sociolinguistic: "Can you help me simplify this part?" "Let's make sure it's easy to understand."</li>
                </ul>
            </td>
            <td style="padding: 8px; border: 1px dashed #333;">15 min</td>
        </tr>
        <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
            <td style="padding: 8px; border: 1px dashed #333;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>STAGE 4 — Performance / Production</b></p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Communicative task where students USE the language in a realistic scenario: "The Talents Around Us"</p>
            </td>
            <td style="padding: 8px; border: 1px dashed #333;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Students work in small groups (3-4 students). Each group receives a "Documentary Scene Card" with a complex task description for their Fiestas Patrias Celebration Documentary (e.g., "Document the various musical talents in the school band, ensuring to capture the individual instruments like drums, flutes, and accordions, and explain their role in the parade performance.").</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Task format:</b> Each group must mediate this complex task into a "Simple Production Plan." This plan will consist of 3-5 numbered, simple written steps, each accompanied by a small drawing or visual aid. Students must use the future simple, first conditional, and the modal 'can' to explain and simplify. They will also include relevant vocabulary (e.g., 'band', 'drums', 'flute', 'accordion', 'perform', 'talent', 'practice', 'parade', 'song', 'music', 'stage'). They are encouraged to use phrases like "If you record the music, the audience will love it," and "We will show the talents." "I can play the drums."</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Groups will present their "Simple Production Plan" to the class, explaining how they simplified the instructions for their documentary crew. They are encouraged to use appropriate cultural expressions like "¡Viva Panamá!" when talking about the celebration.</p>
            </td>
            <td style="padding: 8px; border: 1px dashed #333;">10 min</td>
        </tr>
        <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
            <td style="padding: 8px; border: 1px dashed #333;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>STAGE 5 — Assessment / Post-task</b></p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Formative assessment strategy</p>
            </td>
            <td style="padding: 8px; border: 1px dashed #333;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Assessment Task:</b> Students present their group's "Simple Production Plan" for their documentary scene. The teacher uses an observation checklist to assess students' mediation skills.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Evaluation Criteria (Observation Checklist):</b></p>
                <ul>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Relays information clearly and simply (meditation skill).</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Uses future simple tense for plans (e.g., "We will film...").</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Uses first conditional for possibilities (e.g., "If you interview, you will get good shots.").</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Uses modal 'can' to express ability/talent (e.g., "I can explain...").</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Includes relevant vocabulary (parade, flag, band, costume, talent, practice, perform, honor).</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Uses visuals effectively to support explanations.</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Pronunciation is intelligible (especially short vowels and rhyming words related to Fiestas Patrias).</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Collaborates respectfully with peers (sociolinguistic).</li>
                </ul>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Student Self-Assessment / Exit Ticket:</b> Students complete two sentences on a small slip of paper:</p>
                <ul>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"Today, I learned to simplify instructions for the documentary by..."</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"I can now explain __________ about Fiestas Patrias using simple words."</li>
                </ul>
            </td>
            <td style="padding: 8px; border: 1px dashed #333;">7 min</td>
        </tr>
        <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
            <td style="padding: 8px; border: 1px dashed #333;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>STAGE 6 — Reflection</b></p>
            </td>
            <td style="padding: 8px; border: 1px dashed #333;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Student self-reflection prompt:</b></p>
                <ul>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"What was challenging about simplifying instructions for our Fiestas Patrias documentary today?"</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"How can I use simple words and pictures to explain things to my family or friends about our Panamanian traditions?"</li>
                </ul>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Teacher reflection:</b></p>
                <ul>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">What aspects of explaining and simplifying information (mediation) worked well? Were students able to use visuals effectively?</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">What adjustments or scaffolds might be needed for students who struggled to simplify complex information or integrate the target grammar structures? How can I better support their use of future simple and first conditional in explanations?</li>
                </ul>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Connection to next lesson:</b> This lesson concludes the theme. The next step will be to finalize the Fiestas Patrias Celebration Documentary project based on the simplified plans and potentially present it. This will lead into a new theme and lesson sequence.</p>
            </td>
            <td style="padding: 8px; border: 1px dashed #333;">3 min</td>
        </tr>
    </tbody>
</table>